Wolfi deviation 2 of 2 (docs/deviations.md, "ps-entry.sh pwmake"): MYSQL_RANDOM_ROOT_PASSWORD uses
pwmake (libpwquality, 128 bits of entropy); Wolfi has no libpwquality/pwmake. Replaced with 24 random
bytes from /dev/urandom as 48 hex characters (192 bits of entropy) using od and tr, both busybox
applets already required by the image. Same output contract: one printable, shell-safe string.

--- a/ps-entry.sh	2026-11-13 23:03:20.173083042 +0200
+++ b/ps-entry.sh	2026-11-13 23:03:20.184083032 +0200
@@ -146,7 +146,7 @@
 		fi
 
 		if [ ! -z "$MYSQL_RANDOM_ROOT_PASSWORD" ]; then
-			MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD="$(pwmake 128)"
+			MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD="$(od -An -N24 -tx1 /dev/urandom | tr -d " \n")"
 			echo "GENERATED ROOT PASSWORD: $MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD"
 		fi
 
